# Copy to /opt/fold/backup.env and chmod 600.
# provision.sh never creates the bucket or the key. Backblaze B2 is the
# recommendation. Any S3-compatible bucket works, including DigitalOcean
# Spaces (endpoint https://nyc3.digitaloceanspaces.com, region nyc3).
# Leave this file absent to keep dumps only on the droplet.
#
# When the backup service takes over (provision.sh), these settings are copied into
# .env if .env has none; this file is never changed. KEEP_DAYS here also governs the
# host's originals and their adopted copies. Edit .env afterwards for the service.
#
# The key on this server needs only permission to write objects under fold/
# (S3 PutObject, plus AbortMultipartUpload where it is separate; Backblaze B2
# writeFiles). The scripts never list, read or delete in the bucket. Spaces has no
# write-only key, so its key can also read and delete. Each run uploads into its
# own folder, fold/<stamp>-<random id>/. Keep a read key on your own computer.
#
# Generate the age key on a machine that is not the server:
#   age-keygen -o fold-backup.key
# Put the public key below. Store fold-backup.key in the church password
# manager. The private key must not be copied to the droplet.

FOLD_BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=example-fold-backups
FOLD_BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.us-west-004.backblazeb2.com
FOLD_BACKUP_S3_REGION=us-west-004
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=CHANGE_ME_ACCESS_KEY
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=CHANGE_ME_SECRET
FOLD_BACKUP_AGE_RECIPIENT=age1dryrunexamplepublickeyxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
FOLD_BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS=14
